@startuml
title Appointment and Laboratory Service Integration

actor Doctor
actor "Lab Technician" as Technician
participant "Appointment / Examination\nConsumer :8080" as Consumer
database "Appointment schema" as AppointmentDB
participant "Laboratory Provider :8081" as Laboratory
database "Laboratory schema" as LaboratoryDB

Doctor -> Consumer: POST /api/v1/examinations\n(patientId, appointmentId, testCodes)
activate Consumer
Consumer -> AppointmentDB: Check active patient and scheduled appointment
AppointmentDB --> Consumer: Valid
Consumer -> Laboratory: POST /api/v1/lab-orders\n(Bearer JWT)
activate Laboratory
Laboratory -> LaboratoryDB: Validate test codes and save order
LaboratoryDB --> Laboratory: orderId, RECEIVED
Laboratory --> Consumer: 201 Created
deactivate Laboratory
Consumer -> AppointmentDB: Save examination ↔ labOrderId
alt Consumer persistence succeeds
  AppointmentDB --> Consumer: examinationId
  Consumer --> Doctor: 201 Created
else Consumer persistence fails
  Consumer -> Laboratory: DELETE /api/v1/lab-orders/{id}
  Laboratory -> LaboratoryDB: Mark order CANCELLED
  Laboratory --> Consumer: 204 No Content
  Consumer --> Doctor: 500; order cancellation requested
end
deactivate Consumer

Technician -> Laboratory: PUT /api/v1/lab-orders/{id}/results\n(Bearer JWT)
activate Laboratory
Laboratory -> LaboratoryDB: Save results; mark COMPLETED
LaboratoryDB --> Laboratory: Updated
Laboratory --> Technician: 200 OK
deactivate Laboratory

Doctor -> Consumer: GET /api/v1/examinations/lab-orders/{id}/results
activate Consumer
Consumer -> AppointmentDB: Verify order is linked to an examination
AppointmentDB --> Consumer: Link exists
Consumer -> Laboratory: GET /api/v1/lab-orders/{id}/results\n(Bearer JWT)
activate Laboratory
Laboratory -> LaboratoryDB: Read result
LaboratoryDB --> Laboratory: Result data
Laboratory --> Consumer: 200 OK
deactivate Laboratory
Consumer --> Doctor: 200 OK; result data
deactivate Consumer
@enduml
